  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVEg">IV Eg</ref> 3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-f">Ðæt is þonne, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ic wille, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc mon sy under borge ge binnan burgum ge buton burgu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-c">Ðæt þonne his, þæt ic wille, þæt ælc mann sy under borge ge binnan burgum ge butan burgum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-q">Unusquisque habitans in urbe aut rure sub fideiussore constituatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="3" corresp="#wit-c">Ðæt þonne his þæt ic wille, þæt ælc mann sy under borge ge binnan burgum ge buton burgum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-c">My will is, further, that every man be under surety, whether he live within a borough or in the country.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">Namely, then, it is my will that every man is to be under surety both within the boroughs and outside the boroughs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Nämlich ich will nun, dass jedermann unter Bürgschaft stehe, sowohl innerhalb von Städten, wie ausserhalb von Städten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Namely, I will now that every man be under surety, both within boroughs and outside boroughs.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="211"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_6">III Eg 6</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. III Eg. 6</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="286"><ref target="clause:AGu_4">AGu 4–5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="206"><ref target="clause:IAtr_3">I Atr 3</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares III Eg 6.</note>
      </div>
